{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report", "label": "Task 9 Report: Playwright fidelity harness + desktop comparison", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_playwright_fidelity_harness", "label": "Playwright fidelity harness (shoot.mjs capture + compare.mjs diff)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Captures original bundles (static server) and the built port (next start) at a given width, records geometry/text/font measurements as JSON, and diffs them; replaces eyeball review, which missed several typography defects."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_stray_next_dev_contamination", "label": "Stray next dev process corrupting shared .next build", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A leftover next dev/next start overwrote or served stale .next artifacts mid-capture, making some pages render unstyled; led to the standing habit of an unfiltered process listing and clean rebuild before every capture."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_geometry_tolerance_4px", "label": "4px geometry tolerance for landmark deltas", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Chosen as a small tolerance absorbing sub-pixel font-metric rounding between rendering paths; judgement call, documented inline."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_archivo_wdth_axis_static_instance", "label": "Root cause 1: Archivo loaded as static instances, 'wdth' 106 axis inert", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Explicit weight array in next/font produced static instances without the wdth axis; fixed with axes:['wdth'], proven by width-ratio measurement (1.908 on both targets)."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_body_font_ambiguous_tailwind_utility", "label": "Root cause 2: body font-[var(...)] compiled to --tw-font-weight, not font-family", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Tailwind's ambiguous font- prefix resolved the arbitrary value as a font-weight utility, so body fell back to the system stack; fixed by moving font-family into the globals.css body rule."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_fallback_face_hypothesis_refuted", "label": "Refuted hypothesis: next/font size-adjust fallback faces alter normal line-height", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Round 3 diagnosis; WOFF2 hhea/OS2/head metrics were byte-identical, and the hypothesis was falsified in round 4 when removing next/font left deltas unchanged."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_jetbrains_mono_not_loaded", "label": "JetBrains Mono never loaded in the port (no @font-face or next/font)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measured identical to generic monospace in the port; resolved by self-hosting the original fonts."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_next_font_family_name_mismatch", "label": "Root cause 3: next/font hashed family names never matched markup literal names", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Converted markup references families by real CSS names everywhere; only self-hosting under the real name satisfies that, so next/font was dropped."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_self_hosted_original_fonts", "label": "Self-hosted original WOFF2 fonts (public/fonts + 21 @font-face rules)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "147 @font-face blocks across seven templates deduplicated by resolved text to 21 rules in .source/fonts.css, pasted into globals.css; FONT_FAMILIES allow-list throws on unknown families."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_preflight_html_line_height", "label": "Root cause 4: Tailwind Preflight line-height:1.5 on html", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Elements without explicit leading-* inherited 1.5 instead of normal (14px -> 21px); fixed with html { line-height: normal } in globals.css; explains why only accordion side-lists, hover-card titles and mono labels drifted."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_unlayered_font_inherit_reset", "label": "Root cause 5: unlayered input,textarea,button { font: inherit } beat Tailwind utilities", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Project duplicate of Preflight's reset sat outside @layer, so it overrode every layered utility on form controls (-30px reconciled exactly); deleted since Preflight already provides the same reset inside @layer base."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_css_cascade_layers_unlayered_priority", "label": "CSS Cascade Layers: unlayered rules beat any layered rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "General mechanism established in round 6: unlayered CSS wins regardless of specificity or source order, which is why plain CSS after @import \"tailwindcss\" can silently override utilities."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_real_element_font_proof_guard", "label": "Real-element font rendering regression guard", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Measures real h1 / footer mono span / first paragraph width and height against the original within 1px; replaced synthetic off-DOM checkFontAxis/checkBodyFont guards."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_html_line_height_guard", "label": "html line-height regression guard (expects \"normal\")", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_form_control_guard", "label": "Form control regression guard (textarea font-size, font-family, height)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Strengthened in round 7 to assert fontFamily and height, not only fontSize, since a family-only regression (the round-2 shape) would otherwise pass."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_five_known_acceptable_differences", "label": "Five known-acceptable differences (4 live clock/timer texts + contact body background)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Convergence point of the desktop comparison: diffs 27 -> 26 -> 24 -> 14 -> 5 after five fully reconciled root causes."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_contact_body_background_occlusion", "label": "Contact body background-color #131110 vs #0C0B0A (occluded, ruled no action)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_unfiltered_process_listing", "label": "Unfiltered process listing before every build/capture", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Grepping for the repo path missed stray next start and hung scripts; the readiness check only polls for any 200, so a stale server can masquerade as fresh."}, {"id": "docs_superpowers_reports_task_9_report_portable_out_base_default", "label": "OUT_BASE defaults to os.tmpdir()/arohance-fidelity-shots", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/superpowers/reports/task-9-report.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Review finding: hardcoded personal scratch path replaced so shoot and compare agree on any machine; SHOOT_